## Final Verification Summary

I have successfully verified that the fix works correctly with the following evidence:

### ✅ Primary Fix Verification
The JavaScript test confirms that our URL comparison logic now properly handles case-insensitive hostnames:
- URLs like `"https://example.com/a"` and `"https://EXAMPLE.com/a"` are now correctly identified as matching
- Different URLs like `"https://example.com/a"` and `"https://example.com/b"` are correctly identified as non-matching

### ✅ Regression Testing
All existing tests continue to pass (3/3 tests passing), confirming no functionality was broken.

### ✅ Code Changes
The implementation in `src/import_merge.ts` now:
1. Uses `URL()` constructor to parse both URLs
2. Compares protocol, hostname (case-insensitive), pathname, search, and hash components
3. Falls back to original string comparison if URL parsing fails
4. Maintains all existing functionality

### ✅ Bug Resolution
The specific bug reported - where importing a bookmark whose URL differs from an existing one only by hostname case (e.g., "https://example.com/a" vs "https://EXAMPLE.com/a") - is now fixed. These URLs will be properly merged instead of added as duplicate entries.

The fix is minimal, focused, and maintains backward compatibility while solving the exact issue described in the bug report.

